# One batch of an open-corpus source, observed, each item at its own path under the source's name
# (dn-corpus-instance §5.2). The batch is the next `batch` items past the source's cursor; the
# cursor moves once the batch has landed, so a batch cut off anywhere is read again, whole.
param name, batch = 2000
for it in items(source("corpus/" + name), batch: batch) {
    store it.content in "observed" at "corpus/" + name + "/" + it.id
}
